  "description": "Gravel cycling has exploded recently and it’s no wonder. These bikes are truly do-everything machines, both for beginners and experienced cyclists. We were in the game from the beginning with a gravel bike that had dirt heritage in its DNA. The RAG+ has become a favorite among our employees and friends, even those who would never even consider a drop bar bike before. The range of applications is endless - from commuting to amateur CX racing, or simply to be used as a fitness bike. Multiple mounting points allow you to take anything you need along with you, so the Rag+ is also ready for your next big adventure. RAG is short for Road & Gravel and the 'plus' is there because you can run it with standard 700C road tires, 700C gravel tires (up to 45C) or even 27.5” wheels with tires as big as 2.2”! It features the latest technologies including a proper 1X drivetrain with a wide range cassette, disc brakes and thru-axles. The elegant aluminum frame is complemented with a full carbon fork. The 2022 model has undergone geometry revisions that make this bike more stable and comfortable: the headtubes are taller, placing the rider in a more comfortable position. We didn’t go too far that though – we still want to retain the sporty character of the bike), the reach is longer and head angle is slacker.\nINTENDED USE CATEGORY 2: ROAD & GRAVEL\nRAG is short for Road And Gravel and the 'plus' is there because you can run it with standard 700C road tires, 700C gravel tires (up to 45C) or even 27.5” wheels with tires as big as 2.2”! Perfect for anyone who wants a REAL all round drop bar bike. Use it for bike packing, gravel grinding, amateur CX racing or commuting. If you mount 28mm road tires you can hit the tarmac and easily keep up with your roadie buddies. It features the latest technologies including a proper 1X drivetrain with a wide range cassette, disc brakes and thru-axles.\nNEW FOR 2022:\nrevised geometry (longer head\ntubes, slacker head tube angle)\nrevised frame tubes\nshorter stems 70 / 80 / 90 / 100mm\nFAT VITTORIA Mezcal III 44c TIRES\nflip flop stem\nMAIN FEATURES:\nTough and light alloy frame with bigGer ht in L&xl size\nFull carbon fibre fork\nTubeless compatible wheels\nThru axles front and rear\nSRAM APEX 1X DERAILLEUR\nSRAM APEX Hydraulic brakes\nVITTORIA Mezcal III 44c TLR tires\nClearance for 650B tires up to 2.2\"\nFRAME\nTough and light alloy frame\nTECHNOLOGY\nThru-axles, 1x drivetrains, disc brakes, tubeless ready rims: everything that makes a true modern gravel bike rock!\nHUGE TYRE CLEARANCE\nWTB RADDLER TCS 40c tires\nClearance for 650B tires up to 2.2\"\nUNIQUE DESIGN\nUnique graphic design, hardcore heritage is in the DNA of all NS bikes - even if they have drop bars!",
